WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:06.860
Today we have a proposal from Bernie Sanders
that is an area where he really stands out

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.170
in the democratic field.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.880
It's his plan to get money out of politics.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.120
Now, let's set up the conversation.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:19.769
We've been having a practical discussion here
on this show for a while now about Bernie

00:00:19.769 --> 00:00:22.990
versus Warren on accepting corporate and PAC
money.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:27.039
Now, both Bernie and Warren have turned it
down in primaries.

00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:31.369
Elizabeth Warren has said she would accept
it in the general election saying she doesn't

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:36.640
believe in unilateral disarmament and if this
is the way to win, she thinks we are better

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.980
off with her accepting that money and winning
rather than turning it down and losing and

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.379
seeing Donald Trump reelected.

00:00:43.379 --> 00:00:47.230
Bernie has said he would not accept that money
in the general election and this has become

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:51.219
a sort of battleground on the issue of campaign
finance reform.

00:00:51.219 --> 00:00:53.170
Now I want money out of politics, period.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:56.530
I don't have to qualify it in any other way.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:00.059
Money in politics is a toxic and corrosive
force.

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:01.499
It needs to be done away with.

00:01:01.499 --> 00:01:02.539
It needs to be removed.

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:09.570
It needs to be reformed and I do believe that
it is a conversation to have about whether

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:16.580
by unilaterally disarming in the general election,
you risk losing the election and whether it

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:22.010
is shortsighted in the sense that by getting
into office, if you accept that money in the

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.940
general, you might then be able to change
the system.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.020
Now, this is a theoretical conversation.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.010
I'm not looking to fight anyone over it.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.910
There are reasonable positions to be had on
both sides.

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:39.170
Uh, but I still think that if you win, you
have to work to get rid of campaign of money

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.990
in politics and to change and fix campaign
financing.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:47.340
I don't know that Elizabeth Warren would do
that, but this is a very specific conversation

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.390
to this election about primarily two candidates
of the three front runners.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.770
Biden's certainly not going to do anything
about this.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:59.050
The right thing to do is we need money out
of politics and Bernie Sanders has put out

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:02.790
an absolutely fantastic plan to do it.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:07.710
Bernie's plan is all encompassing in that
it would restructure money in politics when

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:13.270
it comes to parties and conventions and inaugurations,
which by the way, inaugurations for Donald

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:19.700
Trump have served as a great way to funnel
money for influence pedaling for buying influence.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:25.720
Uh, it would restructure a public financing
of elections, primary debate, funding, Congress,

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.720
everything.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.900
So let's look at the details.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:34.600
Number one, Bernie would end corporate contributions
to the democratic convention period.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:39.400
This is already just a great way to set the
tone before you even formally nominate someone.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.260
This is absolutely a, a great thing to be
doing.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:49.890
Bernie would end corporate donations to the
DNC period and two inaugurations and individual

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:50.890
donations.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:55.390
Two inaugurations would be capped at $500
excellent.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:59.630
Bernie would make federal elections publicly
funded.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:01.880
This is like the big boy, right?

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:08.600
This is the real hallmark of any serious plan
to get money out of politics and to fix the

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.490
problems that we have.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:15.160
Bernie would get rid of the federal elections
commission and instead would replace it with

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:20.540
a federal election administration with a governing
body of its own.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:24.870
Bernie also wants a constitutional amendment
to overturn citizens United.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.840
That's not unique to Bernie.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:32.710
Bernie wants to end super packs by legislation
and this is a very interesting component of

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:33.710
the plan.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:40.060
Bernie would install a universal small dollar
voucher system, which would quote, give any

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:45.550
voting age American, the ability to donate
to federal candidates.

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:52.920
This is empowering people in a way that not
only are you democratizing the financing of

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:58.990
elections, you were also, hopefully by getting
people involved in supporting candidates with

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:02.819
money they wouldn't ordinarily even necessarily
have to donate.

00:04:02.819 --> 00:04:05.880
You're making it more likely they're actually
going to participate in the system by voting,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.820
which is a major problem in this country.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:13.349
Uh, Bernie would ban advertising during primary
debates and he would put in place a lifelong

00:04:13.349 --> 00:04:18.519
lobbying ban on former members of Congress
actually doing the thing that Donald Trump

00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:21.389
claimed he would do but hasn't actually done.

00:04:21.389 --> 00:04:22.699
These are the big elements.

00:04:22.699 --> 00:04:24.029
It's not all encompassing.

00:04:24.029 --> 00:04:25.310
There are a few more.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.419
So here's the reality.

00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:32.039
I always want to just talk about the reality
with you and not dance around what it is that's

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:33.680
going on in polling.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:35.819
Elizabeth Warren is surgeon.

00:04:35.819 --> 00:04:40.940
She has overtaken Joe Biden in a number of
recent polls and she may soon overtake the

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:44.070
lead in the 2020 democratic primary.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:48.490
Bernie and Warren are sort of fighting for
the progressive vote.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:54.430
Either would be the most progressive president
that we have ever had, but we can't ignore

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.360
that on this issue.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.990
Bernie is unparalleled in the democratic primary
period.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:01.499
There is no need to qualify it further.

00:05:01.499 --> 00:05:06.389
Every time I say something objective about
Bernie or Warren, people email me, David,

00:05:06.389 --> 00:05:07.389
I'm disappointed.

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:10.819
I'm going to not watch anymore because you
know, I'm a Bernie guy and you're really going

00:05:10.819 --> 00:05:14.689
to Warren or I'm not going to watch any more
because I'm for Warren and now you're just

00:05:14.689 --> 00:05:15.689
propping up Bernie.

00:05:15.689 --> 00:05:16.749
You're a Bernie bro.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:21.650
David, or I'm angry because you're, you know,
hurt trying to hurt Bernie or attacking Warren

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:22.650
or whatever.

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.289
I am communicating the facts.

00:05:24.289 --> 00:05:27.189
Warren is surging in the polls.

00:05:27.189 --> 00:05:30.729
Bernie is unparalleled on this issue of money
in politics.

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:34.059
And this plan is an extraordinarily strong
framework.

00:05:34.059 --> 00:05:39.669
Uh, and to quote Donald Trump, I hope that
whoever is the next president looks at this

00:05:39.669 --> 00:05:44.650
very, very strongly because it is one of the
foremost most issues if we want to really

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:49.479
fix politics, this has to be at the top of
the list along with, of course, climate change

00:05:49.479 --> 00:05:54.680
and dealing with systemic and structural wealth
and income inequality in this country.

